      "text": "Migrate the source-to-rack supply function from powered trolley to hand carrier, using the initial rack stock as the timing buffer. Start nine consecutive hand trips at boundaries 0 through 8, delivering B4 through B12 at boundaries 1 through 9. Inspect continuously from boundary 0, including B9 correction at 8 through 10. Finite-model calculation predicts twelve correct releases at 13, nine source unloads, and nine occupied transfer minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "core_carrier_attack",
      "source_refs": [
        "C2",
        "C3",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "O1",
        "O3",
        "R3",
        "R5",
        "R7"
      ],
      "text": "Attack the migrated carrier dependency through permitted delayed starts: idle the transfer clerk until boundary 3, then hand carry consecutively. First arrival at 4 leaves inspection idle from 3 to 4. Calculation predicts only eleven releases by 13 despite all nine source unloads by 12. The new carrier needs sufficiently early arrivals; freedom from charge does not remove timing dependence."
    },
    {
      "id": "core_rival",
      "source_refs": [
        "C2",
        "C3",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "O1",
        "O4",
        "R2",
        "R3"
      ],
      "text": "Closest rival: trolley B4-B7 from 0 to 3, trolley B8-B11 from 3 to 6, then hand carry B12 from 6 to 7. Boundary ordering permits whole-load unloads without waiting, rack occupancy reaches five, and continuous inspection completes at 13. Predicted transfer occupation is seven minutes. Migration therefore loses the labor preference when both succeed."
    },
    {
      "id": "core_probe",
      "source_refs": [
        "M1",
        "M2",
        "M3",
        "M4",
        "R6",
        "R7",
        "C1"
      ],
      "text": "Check the three declared schedules in the finite event ledger, recording carrier identities, rack occupancy, correct bracket counts and completed seals, occupied intervals, and charge use. Defeat the migration on any inspection gap, blocked unloading that invalidates its timing, or fewer than twelve correct releases at 13. No instrument maintenance labor is modeled."
    }
  ],
